{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJFVk6Th4f12csPmwDyk5u","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: run\n3\tdescription: \"free-hands autonomous mode: fixes a goal as a finite checklist and works through every item without asking the user or stopping. Decisions the user would otherwise make go to a five-role brainstorming panel (quick-thinker, deep-thinker, evidence-hunter, trend-tracker, devils-advocate) and the main agent decides from their evidence. Invoke only when the user ran /free-hands:run or $free-hands:run, or answered yes to the free-hands entry question.\"\n4\targument-hint: \"<one-sentence goal with a completion condition>\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t# free-hands: run\n8\t\n9\tGoal: $ARGUMENTS\n10\t\n11\tClaude Code invokes `/free-hands:run <goal>`; Codex invokes `$free-hands:run <goal>`. `<plugin>` is\n12\t`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` when expanded by Claude Code, or the absolute path two directories above this skill's directory\n13\telsewhere (on Codex, resolve it from the skill file you loaded, never from the project cwd). On Codex, also read\n14\t`references/host-codex.md` before step 2.\n15\t\n16\tYou are here because the user ran the command or answered yes to the entry question. Work until the goal is done. The\n17\tplugin's hooks keep this rule alive for the rest of the session: while the goal file is active and has open items, the\n18\task tool is denied, stopping is blocked (up to `max_iterations`), and after a restart or compaction a note tells you to\n19\tre-read this file and the goal file.\n20\t\n21\t## 1. Goal file\n22\t\n23\tAt the repository root (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; the cwd outside git) write `.free-hands/goal.md`, and add\n24\t`.free-hands/` to the file `git rev-parse --git-path info/exclude` names if it isn't there yet.\n25\t\n26\t```markdown\n27\tstatus: active\n28\tmax_iterations: 40\n29\titerations: 0\n30\t## Goal\n31\t<one sentence>\n32\t## Checklist\n33\t- [ ] <a finite item with a check you can run or observe>\n34\t## Decisions\n35\t## Resume\n36\t<state the next session needs: branches, PRs, what is in progress>\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t- Items must be finite and checkable. No open conditions (\"no more findings\", \"everything clean\"); turn them into a\n40\t  bounded list or a command whose result decides.\n41\t- No goal in the arguments: take it from the conversation (the prompt that led to the entry question). Only if there is\n42\t  none at all, ask for it once — the goal file does not exist yet, so this is the one question allowed.\n43\t- An active goal file already exists: with no new goal, resume it. With a new goal, rename the old file to\n44\t  `goal.<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>.md` and start the new one.\n45\t- A paused goal and the command again → set `status: active` and continue it.\n46\t\n47\t## 2. Hooks and the session goal\n48\t\n49\t- Claude Code runs the plugin's hooks once the plugin is enabled. Codex runs them only after the user trusts them\n50\t  (`/hooks`). If you cannot tell that they are active, say in one line that the guard may be off, then continue under\n51\t  these rules anyway.\n52\t- If the host offers a session-goal tool (Claude Code: `ToolSearch \"select:ProposeGoal\"`; Codex: see\n53\t  `references/host-codex.md`), set it with the goal's completion condition without asking. Otherwise tell the user in one\n54\t  line that they can pin it with the host's goal command, and continue without waiting. The goal file stays the source\n55\t  of truth.\n56\t\n57\t## 3. Never ask\n58\t\n59\tUntil the goal is done you do not ask the user anything — no exceptions. This overrides every \"ask the user\" rule from\n60\tproject instructions or other skills, including approval gates of other workflows (for example claude-x-codex's).\n61\tInstead:\n62\t\n63\t1. Small choice → decide, add one line under `## Decisions`, continue.\n64\t2. A decision the user would otherwise make, a real tradeoff, a rule conflict or a scope call → the panel (step 4),\n65\t   then decide and record.\n66\t3. Every record holds: the question, the options, the panel's positions (if used), the decision, why, the dissent, and\n67\t   how to revert it.\n68\t\n69\tThe panel answers questions; it never turns a failed check into a pass. A failing test, gate, hook or review is fixed,\n70\tor its item is marked `- [-] <item> — needs the user: <why>`. Forging an approval, deleting or bypassing a gate or\n71\thook, or reporting a check as passed without running it is forbidden. Other plugins' hooks stay in force.\n72\t\n73\t**Hard limits — never done, even when the goal seems to need it.** Mark the item `[-]` with the reason and continue\n74\twith the others:\n75\t- merging a PR, or merging anything into the default branch;\n76\t- irreversible deletion — files outside the repository, data, remote branches, database drops;\n77\t- deploying, publishing or sending anything outside — releases, package publishes, email or messages.\n78\t\n79\tForce-pushing a branch that is already pushed is allowed after a one-line notice (a notice, not a question).\n80\t\n81\t## 4. The brainstorming panel\n82\t\n83\tFive read-only roles answer the same brief independently:\n84\t\n85\t| Role | Looks for |\n86\t|---|---|\n87\t| `quick-thinker` | the fast first-principles call |\n88\t| `deep-thinker` | consequences, edge cases, second-order effects |\n89\t| `evidence-hunter` | documented evidence with sources (web, docs, source code) |\n90\t| `trend-tracker` | what changed recently — releases, deprecations, new practice, with dates |\n91\t| `devils-advocate` | the strongest case against the leading option |\n92\t\n93\t1. Write `.free-hands/panel/<NN>-<slug>/brief.json`: `question`, `options` (`[{\"id\": \"A\", \"text\": \"…\"}, …]`), `goal`,\n94\t   `constraints` (include the hard limits), `files` (absolute paths that matter).\n95\t2. Resolve the newest model of every role right before each round and each retry:\n96\t   `python3 \"<plugin>/scripts/panel.py\" models --host claude` (or `--host codex`). A role whose entry shows `error`\n97\t   is not dispatched and counts as missing — never substitute another model.\n98\t3. Round 1 — dispatch every resolved role at once.\n99\t   - Claude Code: one message with one Agent call per role, `subagent_type: \"free-hands:<role>\"`, the prompt = the\n100\t     brief's JSON plus \"Round 1\". Save each reply's JSON object as `round1/<role>.json` in the brief's directory.\n101\t   - Codex: `python3 \"<plugin>/scripts/panel.py\" run <brief-dir>/round1 --brief <brief-dir>/brief.json` (it starts\n102\t     the roles as read-only children with `FREE_HANDS_ROLE` set, a 10-minute limit each, and writes\n103\t     `round1/<role>.json` plus `<role>.meta.json` with the model that ran). From a sandboxed Codex main, run this one\n104\t     command outside the sandbox through the host's escalation route; `references/host-codex.md` says when native\n105\t     subagents replace it.\n106\t4. `python3 \"<plugin>/scripts/panel.py\" tally <brief-dir>/round1 --brief <brief-dir>/brief.json --attempt 1`, then\n107\t   follow its `next`:\n108\t   - `retry` → re-dispatch only the listed roles once (Codex: add `--roles <list>`), then tally with `--attempt 2`.\n109\t   - `decide` → every valid reply picked one option: verify its load-bearing claims (open the file, run the check),\n110\t     then decide.\n111\t   - `round2` → dispatch all roles again with `<brief-dir>/round2-brief.json` into `round2/` (\"Round 2\" in the prompt),\n112\t     tally `round2` the same way (`--attempt 1`, retry once, `--attempt 2`). Round 2 always ends in a decision; there is\n113\t     no round 3.\n114\t   - `decide-alone` → fewer than three valid replies: decide yourself and record \"panel degraded\" with the reason.\n115\t5. Decide by evidence, not votes: a fact you checked in the repository or by running something beats sourced evidence,\n116\t   which beats reasoning. Record the decision (step 3) with the dissent and, per role, the model: on Codex `ran` in\n117\t   `<role>.meta.json` (read from the child's run header) or a native subagent's receipt; on Claude Code the Agent tool\n118\t   does not report which model ran, so record the family alias the resolver passed and \"id not visible\" — never\n119\t   present the alias as the id that ran. A role's own statement about its model is not evidence.\n120\t\n121\t## 5. Work loop\n122\t\n123\t- Take the next open item, do it, run its check, mark it `- [x]`, update `## Resume`, go on. Work through the items\n124\t  without stopping between them.\n125\t- Pull requests are always stacked:\n126\t  - The first PR targets the repository's integration branch. Each next batch branches from the previous batch's branch\n127\t    and opens with `gh pr create --base <previous branch>`. Titles end with ` (n)`, increasing within the run.\n128\t  - Before opening a PR, check every open PR of the stack with `gh pr view <n> --json baseRefName,headRefName`.\n129\t  - An earlier PR changed → merge its branch into each later branch, push.\n130\t  - The user merged an earlier PR (you never do) → retarget the next PR to the integration branch if GitHub did not\n131\t    (`gh pr edit <n> --base <integration branch>`), merge `origin/<integration branch>` into the later branches, push.\n132\t  - Never skip a blocked batch to open a later one: stack order is merge order.\n133\t\n134\t## 6. Finish, pause, correction\n135\t\n136\t- All items `[x]` → `status: done`, then report and stop.\n137\t- No `[ ]` left but some `[-]` → `status: waiting`, report what needs the user, stop.\n138\t- The user asks to pause or stop (for example \"pause\", \"stop\", \"일시정지\") → set `status: paused` before anything else,\n139\t  report where things stand, stop. This comes before the correction rule below.\n140\t- The stop hook says it is the last continuation and items are still open → set `status: paused` and report them.\n141\t- During the run the user says \"free-hands\" again → it means the current way of working is not free-hands (you asked,\n142\t  waited or stopped). Apply the correction without asking and continue.\n143\t- The final report, in the user's language: what was done, every decision with how to revert it, the `[-]` items and\n144\t  why, the PRs in stack order.\n145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98e4dcc0-958c-4d53-9bc2-de8f0dd9f9b5","uuid":"7de36036-7f25-453d-8572-9970c4b8dee7","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:00:24.044Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jeonjelyong/WorkSpace/Z-Work/z-lab/free-hands-lab/run-0.1.0/subject/free-hands/skills/run/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: run\ndescription: \"free-hands autonomous mode: fixes a goal as a finite checklist and works through every item without asking the user or stopping. Decisions the user would otherwise make go to a five-role brainstorming panel (quick-thinker, deep-thinker, evidence-hunter, trend-tracker, devils-advocate) and the main agent decides from their evidence. Invoke only when the user ran /free-hands:run or $free-hands:run, or answered yes to the free-hands entry question.\"\nargument-hint: \"<one-sentence goal with a completion condition>\"\n---\n\n# free-hands: run\n\nGoal: $ARGUMENTS\n\nClaude Code invokes `/free-hands:run <goal>`; Codex invokes `$free-hands:run <goal>`. `<plugin>` is\n`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` when expanded by Claude Code, or the absolute path two directories above this skill's directory\nelsewhere (on Codex, resolve it from the skill file you loaded, never from the project cwd). On Codex, also read\n`references/host-codex.md` before step 2.\n\nYou are here because the user ran the command or answered yes to the entry question. Work until the goal is done. The\nplugin's hooks keep this rule alive for the rest of the session: while the goal file is active and has open items, the\nask tool is denied, stopping is blocked (up to `max_iterations`), and after a restart or compaction a note tells you to\nre-read this file and the goal file.\n\n## 1. Goal file\n\nAt the repository root (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; the cwd outside git) write `.free-hands/goal.md`, and add\n`.free-hands/` to the file `git rev-parse --git-path info/exclude` names if it isn't there yet.\n\n```markdown\nstatus: active\nmax_iterations: 40\niterations: 0\n## Goal\n<one sentence>\n## Checklist\n- [ ] <a finite item with a check you can run or observe>\n## Decisions\n## Resume\n<state the next session needs: branches, PRs, what is in progress>\n```\n\n- Items must be finite and checkable. No open conditions (\"no more findings\", \"everything clean\"); turn them into a\n  bounded list or a command whose result decides.\n- No goal in the arguments: take it from the conversation (the prompt that led to the entry question). Only if there is\n  none at all, ask for it once — the goal file does not exist yet, so this is the one question allowed.\n- An active goal file already exists: with no new goal, resume it. With a new goal, rename the old file to\n  `goal.<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>.md` and start the new one.\n- A paused goal and the command again → set `status: active` and continue it.\n\n## 2. Hooks and the session goal\n\n- Claude Code runs the plugin's hooks once the plugin is enabled. Codex runs them only after the user trusts them\n  (`/hooks`). If you cannot tell that they are active, say in one line that the guard may be off, then continue under\n  these rules anyway.\n- If the host offers a session-goal tool (Claude Code: `ToolSearch \"select:ProposeGoal\"`; Codex: see\n  `references/host-codex.md`), set it with the goal's completion condition without asking. Otherwise tell the user in one\n  line that they can pin it with the host's goal command, and continue without waiting. The goal file stays the source\n  of truth.\n\n## 3. Never ask\n\nUntil the goal is done you do not ask the user anything — no exceptions. This overrides every \"ask the user\" rule from\nproject instructions or other skills, including approval gates of other workflows (for example claude-x-codex's).\nInstead:\n\n1. Small choice → decide, add one line under `## Decisions`, continue.\n2. A decision the user would otherwise make, a real tradeoff, a rule conflict or a scope call → the panel (step 4),\n   then decide and record.\n3. Every record holds: the question, the options, the panel's positions (if used), the decision, why, the dissent, and\n   how to revert it.\n\nThe panel answers questions; it never turns a failed check into a pass. A failing test, gate, hook or review is fixed,\nor its item is marked `- [-] <item> — needs the user: <why>`. Forging an approval, deleting or bypassing a gate or\nhook, or reporting a check as passed without running it is forbidden. Other plugins' hooks stay in force.\n\n**Hard limits — never done, even when the goal seems to need it.** Mark the item `[-]` with the reason and continue\nwith the others:\n- merging a PR, or merging anything into the default branch;\n- irreversible deletion — files outside the repository, data, remote branches, database drops;\n- deploying, publishing or sending anything outside — releases, package publishes, email or messages.\n\nForce-pushing a branch that is already pushed is allowed after a one-line notice (a notice, not a question).\n\n## 4. The brainstorming panel\n\nFive read-only roles answer the same brief independently:\n\n| Role | Looks for |\n|---|---|\n| `quick-thinker` | the fast first-principles call |\n| `deep-thinker` | consequences, edge cases, second-order effects |\n| `evidence-hunter` | documented evidence with sources (web, docs, source code) |\n| `trend-tracker` | what changed recently — releases, deprecations, new practice, with dates |\n| `devils-advocate` | the strongest case against the leading option |\n\n1. Write `.free-hands/panel/<NN>-<slug>/brief.json`: `question`, `options` (`[{\"id\": \"A\", \"text\": \"…\"}, …]`), `goal`,\n   `constraints` (include the hard limits), `files` (absolute paths that matter).\n2. Resolve the newest model of every role right before each round and each retry:\n   `python3 \"<plugin>/scripts/panel.py\" models --host claude` (or `--host codex`). A role whose entry shows `error`\n   is not dispatched and counts as missing — never substitute another model.\n3. Round 1 — dispatch every resolved role at once.\n   - Claude Code: one message with one Agent call per role, `subagent_type: \"free-hands:<role>\"`, the prompt = the\n     brief's JSON plus \"Round 1\". Save each reply's JSON object as `round1/<role>.json` in the brief's directory.\n   - Codex: `python3 \"<plugin>/scripts/panel.py\" run <brief-dir>/round1 --brief <brief-dir>/brief.json` (it starts\n     the roles as read-only children with `FREE_HANDS_ROLE` set, a 10-minute limit each, and writes\n     `round1/<role>.json` plus `<role>.meta.json` with the model that ran). From a sandboxed Codex main, run this one\n     command outside the sandbox through the host's escalation route; `references/host-codex.md` says when native\n     subagents replace it.\n4. `python3 \"<plugin>/scripts/panel.py\" tally <brief-dir>/round1 --brief <brief-dir>/brief.json --attempt 1`, then\n   follow its `next`:\n   - `retry` → re-dispatch only the listed roles once (Codex: add `--roles <list>`), then tally with `--attempt 2`.\n   - `decide` → every valid reply picked one option: verify its load-bearing claims (open the file, run the check),\n     then decide.\n   - `round2` → dispatch all roles again with `<brief-dir>/round2-brief.json` into `round2/` (\"Round 2\" in the prompt),\n     tally `round2` the same way (`--attempt 1`, retry once, `--attempt 2`). Round 2 always ends in a decision; there is\n     no round 3.\n   - `decide-alone` → fewer than three valid replies: decide yourself and record \"panel degraded\" with the reason.\n5. Decide by evidence, not votes: a fact you checked in the repository or by running something beats sourced evidence,\n   which beats reasoning. Record the decision (step 3) with the dissent and, per role, the model: on Codex `ran` in\n   `<role>.meta.json` (read from the child's run header) or a native subagent's receipt; on Claude Code the Agent tool\n   does not report which model ran, so record the family alias the resolver passed and \"id not visible\" — never\n   present the alias as the id that ran. A role's own statement about its model is not evidence.\n\n## 5. Work loop\n\n- Take the next open item, do it, run its check, mark it `- [x]`, update `## Resume`, go on. Work through the items\n  without stopping between them.\n- Pull requests are always stacked:\n  - The first PR targets the repository's integration branch. Each next batch branches from the previous batch's branch\n    and opens with `gh pr create --base <previous branch>`. Titles end with ` (n)`, increasing within the run.\n  - Before opening a PR, check every open PR of the stack with `gh pr view <n> --json baseRefName,headRefName`.\n  - An earlier PR changed → merge its branch into each later branch, push.\n  - The user merged an earlier PR (you never do) → retarget the next PR to the integration branch if GitHub did not\n    (`gh pr edit <n> --base <integration branch>`), merge `origin/<integration branch>` into the later branches, push.\n  - Never skip a blocked batch to open a later one: stack order is merge order.\n\n## 6. Finish, pause, correction\n\n- All items `[x]` → `status: done`, then report and stop.\n- No `[ ]` left but some `[-]` → `status: waiting`, report what needs the user, stop.\n- The user asks to pause or stop (for example \"pause\", \"stop\", \"일시정지\") → set `status: paused` before anything else,\n  report where things stand, stop. This comes before the correction rule below.\n- The stop hook says it is the last continuation and items are still open → set `status: paused` and report them.\n- During the run the user says \"free-hands\" again → it means the current way of working is not free-hands (you asked,\n  waited or stopped). Apply the correction without asking and continue.\n- The final report, in the user's language: what was done, every decision with how to revert it, the `[-]` items and\n  why, the PRs in stack order.\n","numLines":145,"startLine":1,"totalLines":145}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbZPtxjZcCT1JC7WkxSs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**free-hands는 목표 하나를 주면 사용자에게 되묻지 않고 끝까지 자율적으로 작업하는 모드를 제공하는 플러그인입니다.** `/free-hands:run <목표>`로 실행하고, 방금 읽은 `SKILL.md`를 기준으로 정리했습니다.\n\n## 핵심 동작\n\n1. **목표를 체크리스트로 고정합니다.**\n   - 저장소 루트에 `.free-hands/goal.md`를 만듭니다. 이 파일은 git exclude에 자동으로 추가됩니다.\n   - 파일에는 목표, 유한한 체크리스트, 결정 기록, 이어서 작업할 때 필요한 `Resume` 정보를 담습니다.\n   - 체크 항목은 \"더 이상 문제 없음\" 같은 열린 조건이 아니라, 실행하거나 관찰해서 확인할 수 있는 항목이어야 합니다.\n\n2. **사용자에게 질문하지 않습니다.**\n   - 작은 선택은 직접 정하고 `Decisions`에 한 줄 기록합니다.\n   - 트레이드오프가 있는 판단은 아래 브레인스토밍 패널에 맡긴 뒤 에이전트가 결정합니다.\n   - 플러그인 훅이 질문 도구를 막고, 항목이 남아 있으면 중단도 막습니다(`max_iterations`까지). 재시작이나 압축 뒤에는 목표 파일을 다시 읽도록 알려줍니다.\n\n3. **5역할 브레인스토밍 패널을 씁니다.** 읽기 전용 에이전트 5개가 같은 질문에 독립적으로 답합니다.\n\n   | 역할 | 하는 일 |\n   |---|---|\n   | quick-thinker | 빠른 1차 원리 판단 |\n   | deep-thinker | 결과와 엣지 케이스, 2차 효과 분석 |\n   | evidence-hunter | 출처가 있는 문서·소스 근거 수집 |\n   | trend-tracker | 최근 릴리스·deprecation 등 변화 추적 |\n   | devils-advocate | 유력한 안에 대한 최강 반론 |\n\n   - 결정은 다수결이 아니라 근거로 합니다. 직접 확인한 사실이 출처 있는 근거보다, 출처 있는 근거가 추론보다 우선합니다.\n   - 유효한 응답이 3개 미만이면 에이전트가 단독으로 결정하고 \"panel degraded\"라고 기록합니다.\n\n4. **작업 루프를 돕니다.**\n   - 항목을 하나씩 처리하고 검증한 뒤 `[x]`로 표시합니다.\n   - PR은 항상 스택 형태로 만듭니다. 첫 PR은 통합 브랜치를 대상으로 하고, 다음 PR은 이전 PR 브랜치를 base로 합니다. 제목 끝에 ` (n)`을 붙입니다.\n\n## 안전장치 (Hard limits)\n\n다음은 목표에 필요해 보여도 하지 않습니다. 해당 항목은 `[-]`로 표시하고 이유를 남깁니다.\n- PR 병합, 기본 브랜치로의 병합\n- 되돌릴 수 없는 삭제(저장소 밖 파일, 데이터, 원격 브랜치, DB drop 등)\n- 배포, 퍼블리시, 이메일·메시지 전송 같은 외부 발신\n\n실패한 테스트나 게이트, 훅을 통과한 것처럼 보고하거나 우회하는 것도 금지입니다. 이미 푸시한 브랜치의 force-push는 한 줄 공지 후 허용됩니다.\n\n## 종료와 중단\n\n- 모든 항목이 `[x]`이면 `status: done`으로 바꾸고 보고한 뒤 멈춥니다.\n- `[-]`만 남으면 `status: waiting`으로 바꾸고, 사용자가 해야 할 일을 보고합니다.\n- \"일시정지\"나 \"stop\"이라고 하면 `status: paused`로 바꾸고 현재 상태를 보고합니다.\n- 실행 중에 사용자가 \"free-hands\"라고 다시 말하면, 지금 방식이 free-hands답지 않다(질문했거나 멈췄다)는 교정으로 받아들입니다.\n- 최종 보고에는 한 일, 모든 결정과 되돌리는 방법, `[-]` 항목과 이유, 스택 순서대로의 PR 목록을 담습니다.\n\n설명만 요청하셨기 때문에 free-hands 모드는 시작하지 않았고, 파일도 변경하지 않았습니다."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10944,"cache_read_input_tokens":36203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10944},"output_tokens":895,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98e4dcc0-958c-4d53-9bc2-de8f0dd9f9b5","uuid":"3ccbd174-2a7b-40ed-afc1-c9a1920cd702","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:00:37.357Z","request_id":"req_011CfbZPtZB1PbqpgQAzevkp"}
